# Azure China: provisioned, and three real parity gaps found

The wiring in the entry above was untested — no Azure China access. With a China
account signed in (`Databricks Mooncake Field Test`, chinanorth3), it was
provisioned for real. Three things the documentation-based guesses got wrong.

## 1. Docker Hub is unreachable from Azure China

`FROM python:3.11-slim-bookworm` fails in the ACR build agent:

    Get "https://registry-1.docker.io/v2/": request canceled while waiting for
    connection (Client.Timeout exceeded while awaiting headers)

And ACR's own **server-side** `az acr import` from Docker Hub fails too, with
HTTP 424 Failed Dependency — so the usual "import it into your registry first"
workaround does not work either, at least not from Docker Hub.

What does work: **MCR's Docker Hub mirror**,
`mcr.microsoft.com/mirror/docker/library/python:3.11-slim-bookworm`, which is the
*identical* image, and `ghcr.io/astral-sh/uv` imports fine.

`deploy/azure/Dockerfile` gained `BASE_IMAGE` and `UV_IMAGE` build args defaulting
to the public images, so a global build is unchanged and China passes its ACR-local
imports. Verified: the build succeeds in 2m33s, which also proves the build agent
*can* reach Debian's apt mirrors and `files.pythonhosted.org`.

A second issue surfaced doing this: `COPY --from=${UV_IMAGE}` fails on ACR's
classic builder with *"invalid from flag value ${UV_IMAGE}"* — it does not expand
an ARG inside a `--from` flag, though `FROM ${ARG}` is expanded. uv now arrives via
a named stage (`FROM ${UV_IMAGE} AS uvbin`), which works on both builders.

## 2. Entra-only PostgreSQL is rejected

`--microsoft-entra-auth Enabled --password-auth Disabled` fails:

    (MissingRequiredParameter) Parameter 'AdministratorLoginPassword' must be
    specified.

Azure China still demands a password admin even when disabling password auth. The
server was created with both enabled and a random unused admin password (the app
authenticates with an Entra token; the password is never used and is not recorded).
The China README now documents this rather than the Entra-only form that works
globally.

## 3. CLI flag parity

`az postgres flexible-server db create` takes `--name`, not `-d`, and
`firewall-rule create` needs `--server-name`. Same class of drift as the global
deployment hit earlier this release.

## What the code changes bought

The suffix-derived audience worked exactly as intended. Against the real server:

    PGHOST=ontobricks-pg-cn.postgres.database.chinacloudapi.cn
    audience  -> https://ossrdbms-aad.database.chinacloudapi.cn/.default
    auth mode -> entra

and a `psql` connection with a token for that audience **succeeded** —
`connected as steve.shao@DatabricksTest.partner.onmschina.cn`, server 16.15. So the
audience value guessed from documentation was right, and no configuration beyond
`PGHOST` was needed.

## Provisioned in ontobricks-cn-rg / chinanorth3

| Resource | Name |
|---|---|
| Registry | `ontobrickscn.azurecr.cn` |
| PostgreSQL 16 | `ontobricks-pg-cn.postgres.database.chinacloudapi.cn`, Entra + password auth, db `ontobricks` |
| AKS | `ontobricks-aks-cn`, OIDC issuer + workload identity **both supported** |
| Managed identity | `ontobricks-app-identity`, federated to `system:serviceaccount:ontobricks:ontobricks` |
| Image | `ontobricks:dbaeafcb` |

The identity is a Postgres principal via `pgaadauth_create_principal` with
`CREATE ON DATABASE` (verified `true`), so the app can create its registry and
graph schemas.

## A design mistake I made and corrected

I filled the real client id into the **shared** `serviceaccount.yaml`. That base is
used by every overlay, so a global-cloud deploy from it would have authenticated as
the China identity. Moved to `overlays/china/serviceaccount-china.yaml`; the base
keeps a placeholder, and two tests now enforce the split — one that the base
contains `REPLACE`, one that the overlay carries a real GUID.

## Not done

`kubectl apply -k` was not run. A hook blocks this agent from invoking `kubectl` at
all, including `kustomize` and `--dry-run=client`, and I did not route around it.
The overlay is filled in with real values and the command is in the README.

